WEBVTT

00:00:00.084 --> 00:00:01.611
Newton lost a fortune.

00:00:01.621 --> 00:00:02.752
Supposedly.

00:00:02.762 --> 00:00:07.630
In 1720, South Sea Company shares soared

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:10.450
from £128 to about £1,000.

00:00:10.579 --> 00:00:12.794
Newton wasn't just any investor.

00:00:12.804 --> 00:00:14.628
He was Master of the Mint.

00:00:14.638 --> 00:00:15.412
The story:

00:00:15.422 --> 00:00:18.254
Newton sold at a profit, bought back

00:00:18.264 --> 00:00:20.178
higher and lost £20,000.

00:00:20.278 --> 00:00:22.386
He supposedly said he could calculate the

00:00:22.396 --> 00:00:24.921
heavens but not the madness of people.

00:00:24.946 --> 00:00:25.647
True?

00:00:25.657 --> 00:00:26.347
Maybe.

00:00:26.357 --> 00:00:29.297
The quote is secondhand,
and Oxford's Newton

00:00:29.307 --> 00:00:31.835
project says he likely lost money, but

00:00:31.845 --> 00:00:34.282
the evidence is inconclusive.
